284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 64 0 R
/T (App-A to App-B: App-A sends ICMP traffic to 10.20.1.10. The route table associated with App-A's subnet sends destination 10.20.0.0/16 to the VPC peering connection. VPC B's route table sends return traffic for 10.10.0.0/16 back through the same peering connection. The App-B security group must allow the ICMP request from App-A's private IP. Laptop to App-B administration: the laptop initiates SSH to the bastion's public IPv4 address. SSH ProxyJump then opens a separate SSH connection from the bastion to App-B's private address 10.20.1.10. This requires the VPC A public route table to route 10.20.0.0/16 to the peering connection, the VPC B return route to VPC A, and security group rules that permit SSH from the bastion's private IP.)
/E (App-A to App-B: App-A sends ICMP traffic to 10.20.1.10. The route table associated with App-A's subnet sends destination 10.20.0.0/16 to the VPC peering connection. VPC B's route table sends return traffic for 10.10.0.0/16 back through the same peering connection. The App-B security group must allow the ICMP request from App-A's private IP. Laptop to App-B administration: the laptop initiates SSH to the bastion's public IPv4 address. SSH ProxyJump then opens a separate SSH connection from the bastion to App-B's private address 10.20.1.10. This requires the VPC A public route table to route 10.20.0.0/16 to the peering connection, the VPC B return route to VPC A, and security group rules that permit SSH from the bastion's private IP.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
